From: Christian Marangi <ansuelsmth@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 13:34:14 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] net: ethernet: qualcomm: select PPE and PCS build dependencies

Fix unmet dependency with QCOM_PPE on selecting SFP.

The config symbol for the PCS driver has changed to PCS_QCOM_IPQ9574, since
the original submission. Update Kconfig accordingly.

Merged from:
  0340-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-Fix-unmet-dependency-with-.patch
  0341-net-ethernet-qualcomm-ppe-select-correct-PCS-depende.patch

Based on work by:
  Alexandru Gagniuc <mr.nuke.me@gmail.com>
  Christian Marangi <ansuelsmth@gmail.com>

Original-commit: 7e872efc79091d4b43983d10a28ba322195f9d76
Original-commit: e913a488e9c8f338488eaa5b3a88e10dffb4e7ee

Signed-off-by: Christian Marangi <ansuelsmth@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: Alexandru Gagniuc <mr.nuke.me@gmail.com>
Signed-off-by: ViKing <viking.yfy@qq.com>

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/Kconfig
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/qualcomm/Kconfig
@@ -66,8 +66,7 @@ config QCOM_PPE
 	depends on ARCH_QCOM || COMPILE_TEST
 	select REGMAP_MMIO
 	select PHYLINK
-	select PCS_QCOM_IPQ_UNIPHY
-	select SFP
+	select PCS_QCOM_IPQ9574
 	help
 	  This driver supports the Qualcomm Technologies, Inc. packet
 	  process engine (PPE) available with IPQ SoC. The PPE includes
